@id=areas-for-reading-epics-for-work @kind=decision
Feature: Features are filed by area; an epic names its work and goes once it is built

  Not durable epics or packs, which outlive their work and come to gather all of it, nor an area tag,
  which repeats a folder: a feature lives in the folder of its area, which readers browse and
  CODEOWNERS routes, and an epic names the work toward one outcome with `@includes:`, from a folder
  named for it in its area's backlog, beside the features still to come it groups, when that work is
  one area's, and from the plan when it spans areas. The price is that sdp reads no meaning into an
  area or an epic's folder, and that an epic is kept true and deleted by hand: a feature leaves the
  epic's folder when it is built, and the epic still names it until all of its work is.
